#conversation file
version=0.1

question "Hey. It's been a while." {
    tag=Normal
    answer=Since the ward. Since visiting hours and the vending machine coffee that tasted like a punishment.
    answer=Since you were the only person in that whole building who didn't look at me like I was made of glass.

    question "How have you been, really?" {
        tag=Normal
        answer=Some days I'm a person. Some days I'm just a body that remembered how to get dressed.
        answer=Today's somewhere in between. That's probably why I said yes to this.

        question "Can we talk? Like we said we would, back on the ward." {
            tag=Normal
            answer=Yeah. I've been waiting for someone to actually ask.
            answer=Okay. Go ahead. I'll try not to fold up on you.

            question "What actually happened? What led you here?" {
                tag=NormalFace
                sets=AskedEvent
                answer=I was starting to disappear from a mirror I used to love. That's the easiest way I can put it.
                answer=The testosterone gave me a jaw, a voice, everything I'd begged my body for since I was small -- and it took my hair in exchange, strand by strand, like a toll I hadn't read the terms of.
                answer=Then he left. And some door in me that had been barely holding just came off its hinge.
                answer=I don't remember deciding anything. I remember the mirror. Then I remember waking up in a bed three feet from yours, both of us wired to the same quiet machines.

                question "That took real courage to say out loud." {
                    tag=Normal
                    sets=Kind
                    answer=...
                    answer=Nobody's said that to me yet. Everyone else just goes quiet, like I handed them something breakable.
                    answer=Thank you. For not flinching.
                }
            }

            question "I don't want to talk about the hospital." {
                tag=Normal
                sets=Avoidant
                answer=Oh.
                answer=Okay. That's -- okay.
                answer=I've been carrying it around for months hoping someone would let me put it down. I guess not today.
            }

            question "Honestly? All this over losing a boyfriend and some hair?" {
                tag=Normal
                ending
                ending_text=Tiago didn't cry. That was somehow worse than if he had.
                ending_text=He just said "okay," quietly, and started collecting his coat, his bag, every small proof he'd been sitting there at all.
                ending_text=We haven't spoken since. I still have his number saved as "Tiago (ward)." I can't bring myself to change it, or to use it.
                answer=...okay. I think I should go.
            }

            question "Were you scared, when they admitted you?" {
                tag=HospitalScene
                requires=AskedEvent
                sets=Kind
                answer=Terrified. Not of dying -- I'd already made my peace with that part, which is its own kind of terrifying to say.
                answer=Scared they'd put me on the wrong ward. Scared of the wrong name on a wristband, the wrong pronoun from a tired nurse at 3am.
                answer=Then I saw you two beds down, and some of it went quiet. Not all of it. Some.

                question "What was the scariest part, looking back?" {
                    tag=HospitalScene
                    answer=The mornings. The ten seconds every morning where I had to remember why I was there.
                    answer=You'd already be awake by then, most days. Watching the door like you were guarding it for both of us.
                }
            }

            question "You don't have to carry that alone, you know." {
                tag=Normal
                requires=AskedEvent
                sets=Kind
                answer=I know. I'm still learning how to believe it.
                answer=It helps, hearing you say it. It actually helps.
            }

            question "Can I tell you something? Something I probably shouldn't." {
                tag=NormalFace
                requires=Kind
                answer=I've been trying to find the right moment for months. I don't think there is one. So.
                answer=You were the only good thing in that building. The only reason I didn't spend every hour in there wishing I'd finished what I started.
                answer=I think I'm in love with you. I have been for a long time now.

                question "I care about you so much, Tiago. Just -- not like that." {
                    tag=NormalFace
                    answer=...
                    answer=Yeah. I think some part of me already knew. I just needed to say it once, out loud, to a real person.
                    answer=Thank you for not making it weird. And for still being here after I said it.
                }
            }

            question "I'm really glad we got to talk properly." {
                tag=Normal
                ending
                requires=Kind
                ending_text=Tiago owns a small bakery now, three blocks from the hospital neither of us likes driving past.
                ending_text=He still has bad weeks. Still has a scar or two that surface on the worst of them.
                ending_text=But he unlocks the door at six every morning anyway, flour on his hands instead of a razor, and some mornings that's the whole entire victory.
                answer=Me too. Thank you for not treating me like a story you already knew the ending to.
            }

            question "I hope things get easier for you." {
                tag=Normal
                ending
                requires_not=Kind
                requires=Avoidant
                ending_text=I got the call on a Tuesday. I don't remember much else about that day.
                ending_text=I keep thinking about the hospital doors we both walked out of, years ago, and how I let him walk back toward one alone.
                ending_text=He wanted to talk about it. I never let him. I don't think I'll ever stop paying for that.
                answer=Thanks. I'll try.
            }

            question "Thank you for talking with me." {
                tag=Normal
                ending
                requires_not=Kind
                requires_not=Avoidant
                ending_text=Tiago is back in a hospital bed tonight, three floors up from where we first met.
                ending_text=I visited. Brought the bad vending machine coffee, like old times. He managed a small, tired smile at that.
                ending_text=We didn't talk about much. Maybe next time. There's always a maybe next time, until the day there isn't.
                answer=Thanks for coming. It was good to see you.
            }
        }
    }
}
